    {
      "beat_id": "B00",
      "act": "OPEN",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16.0,
      "narration_text": "You built a tool that reads financial numbers out of filings. How do you know it's right? You don't — until you benchmark it. When I grew my test set from two companies to ten, it caught three real bugs I could not see.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "My extractor passes on two companies. Is it actually correct?",
            "topic": "HUMANITARIANS AI · MYCROFT",
            "segment": "Trust, but Verify",
            "greeting": "Selam, Kore",
            "runningText": "scaling the test…",
            "output": [
              "Two passing companies prove almost nothing.",
              "Build an independent golden set; score it.",
              "Scaling 2 → 10 companies caught three real bugs."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "modelLabel": "Fable 5",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B00.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B00.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.33,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B00.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-10-31T21:06:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01B",
      "act": "Why This Matters",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22.0,
      "narration_text": "Hi, I'm Asavari, a fellow at Humanitarians AI. This video is about how a benchmark moved my SEC Filings agent from specified to verified, by catching three real bugs when I scaled the test from two companies to ten. You'll see what a golden set is, how the bugs hid in plain sight, and why forty-six out of forty-six only means something because of how it's measured. If you ship an automated pipeline, this is for you.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "What is this video about, and why should I watch it?",
            "topic": "HUMANITARIANS AI · MYCROFT",
            "segment": "Trust, but Verify",
            "greeting": "Hi, I'm Asavari",
            "runningText": "the one-line summary…",
            "output": [
              "Who: Asavari, a Humanitarians AI fellow",
              "What: how a benchmark took the agent specified → verified",
              "Why watch: a passing number is only as good as its test"
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "modelLabel": "Fable 5",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01B.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "tangent": true,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01B.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 26.07,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01B.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-10-31T21:06:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "THE PROBLEM",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22.0,
      "narration_text": "Two companies passing tells you almost nothing. A pipeline can look perfect and still be wrong on the eleventh filing — a different tag, a different layout, an edge case you never tried. Confidence without a hard, independent test isn't verification. It's a demo.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeWindow",
          "props": {
            "view": "artifact",
            "artifactTitle": "Two passing companies prove almost nothing",
            "artifactHeading": "looks perfect, wrong on the 11th",
            "artifactLines": [
              "A pipeline can pass a demo and fail an edge case",
              "different tag, different layout, untried filing",
              "confidence without a hard test is a demo, not proof"
            ],
            "sparkLine": "A demo is not verification."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 16.79,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-10-31T21:06:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "THE MECHANISM",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 28.0,
      "narration_text": "So I built a golden set: expected values for each company and metric, sourced independently of the tool, across ten companies and several sectors. The benchmark scores two things — coverage, did we find the value at all, and accuracy, is it within a strict tolerance, half a percent. And a value we can't find is marked MISSING, a flagged gap, never a silent zero.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeWindow",
          "props": {
            "view": "artifact",
            "artifactTitle": "A golden set, scored two ways",
            "artifactHeading": "coverage + accuracy, independently sourced",
            "artifactLines": [
              "Expected values sourced independently of the tool",
              "Coverage: found it at all?  Accuracy: within 0.5%?",
              "Not found → MISSING (a flagged gap), never a silent zero"
            ],
            "sparkLine": "Independent, strict, honest."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 22.38,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-10-31T21:06:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "THE FINDINGS",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 26.0,
      "narration_text": "Scaling from two companies to ten caught three real bugs, each invisible at two. One company had changed its XBRL tag across years, so the latest number was silently lost. One ticker resolved to an empty shell entity with no filings. And several filers reported no single total-liabilities tag at all. I fixed each one, and re-ran.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeWindow",
          "props": {
            "view": "artifact",
            "artifactTitle": "Scaling 2 → 10 caught three real bugs",
            "artifactHeading": "each one invisible at two companies",
            "artifactLines": [
              "Tag migration: the latest value silently lost across years",
              "Ticker resolved to an empty shell entity (no filings)",
              "No aggregate total-liabilities tag for some filers"
            ],
            "sparkLine": "The test found what I couldn't."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 22.63,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-10-31T21:06:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "The verdict",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16.0,
      "narration_text": "The result: forty-six of forty-six metrics match, within half a percent, across ten companies. But that number only earns trust because the test is independent, hard enough to fail, and honest about what it can't resolve. A benchmark isn't paperwork. It's how you earn the right to say verified.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
